# Introduction to the Keymaps of 99.lua

Welcome to the **99.lua** keymap guide! `99.lua` integrates powerful AI-driven development workflows directly into your Neovim workspace. It provides seamless interaction modes, visual prompt selection, custom worker workflows, and model/provider selection.

All `99.lua` keymaps are bound under the `<leader>9` prefix to prevent conflicts with other Neovim bindings. By default, your `<leader>` key is set to `<Space>`.

---

## 🛠️ Essential Keymaps

| Keybinding | Mode | Function | Description |
| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |
| `<leader>9v` | **Visual** | `_99.visual()` | Sends your current visual selection to `99.lua` as context for a prompt. |
| `<leader>9x` | **Normal** | `_99.stop_all_requests()` | Aborts/cancels all currently active/pending AI requests. |
| `<leader>9s` | **Normal** | `_99.search()` | Launches the `99.lua` search tool for workspace-wide queries. |
| `<leader>9V` | **Normal** | `_99.vibe()` | Activates the developer vibe interface (`_99.vibe()`). |
| `<leader>9h` | **Normal** | `_99.open()` | Re-opens your previous AI request history (`99: Open previous request`). |
| `<leader>9t` | **Normal** | `_99.tutorial()` | Launches the interactive `99.lua` tutorial (`99: Interactive Tutorial`). |

---

## 🗺️ Telescope Extensions (Model & Provider Selection)
You can dynamically configure your LLM model and provider in real-time using Telescope picker integration.

| Keybinding | Mode | Function | Description |
| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |
| `<leader>9m` | **Normal** | `select_model()` | Select from available LLM models using Telescope. |
| `<leader>9p` | **Normal** | `select_provider()` | Select from configured LLM providers (e.g. Gemini CLI, OpenCode). |

---

## 👷 Worker Extensions
The Worker module lets you set and track units of work within Neovim.

| Keybinding | Mode | Function | Description |
| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |
| `<leader>9w` | **Normal** | `set_work()` | Define/set a current work item. |
| `<leader>9ws`| **Normal** | `search()` | Search and view remaining work items. |

---

## 💡 Pro-Tips for using `99.lua`
1. **Visual Selection Safety**: The `<leader>9v` mapping is explicitly restricted to **Visual Mode** (`v` mode) to guarantee that you only send the exact text you currently have highlighted, avoiding accidents with older or stale visual selections.
2. **Graceful Cancellations**: If you make a request that is taking too long or you want to abort, immediately hit `<leader>9x` to stop all requests and free up resources.
3. **Interactive Help**: Ready to practice? Press `<leader>9t` inside Neovim to start the official built-in interactive tutorial!
